.TH SDL_SetSurfaceColorspace 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetSurfaceColorspace \- Set the colorspace used by a surface.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_surface.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetSurfaceColorspace(SDL_Surface *surface, SDL_Colorspace colorspace);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Setting the colorspace doesn\(aqt change the pixels, only how they are interpreted in color operations\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I surface
the
.BR SDL_Surface
structure to update\[char46]
.TP
.I colorspace
an
.BR SDL_Colorspace
value describing the surface colorspace\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function can be called on different threads with different surfaces\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetSurfaceColorspace (3)
